hey everybody my name is mayuko and  welcome back to my channel where we talk  about tech  career and life so we've been  quarantining for months at this point  and i feel like i've got kind of a  routine down for  my work day so today in this video i'm  going to show you my work from home  routine in  quarantine so let's get started so on  work days i usually wake up anywhere  between 7 45  and 8 15. so as part of waking up i  brush my teeth i wash my face  and i get dressed for the day and on  some days of the week  i'll work out before my work day i'm  usually more of like a evening workout  person but  i've been working out in the mornings  recently and it's been really helping to  ground me  and improve my mental health during this  weird time  and at 9 00 a.m i have my daily stand-up  so i work for myself now but one thing  that i really miss  about working at a company or at an  office is just kind of the regular  routine of seeing co-workers every day  and so a couple of friends and i started  this daily stand-up group for ourselves  we're all creative professionals who've  had careers in the tech industry  so we meet monday through friday at 9 00  am for about 15 minutes to do  a stand-up in each stand-up we talk  about what we did yesterday and what  we're doing today  and it's been a really good structure  for accountability and an incredible  support group  so after stand-up is over i do kind of  the rest of my morning routine  between showering after my workout  eating breakfast  and taking my dog for a walk so all in  all it takes me about two hours to get  ready for the day  which does feel a little bit long  especially given that i don't need a  commute anywhere  but those two hours are really precious  in that it helps me to context switch  from being  at home to kind of like a work mode  because especially if we're not changing  our surroundings then it's the mindset  and mentality that needs to change  and so during that two hours i slowly  but surely kind of get myself  into that mode so then at around 10 a.m  i sit down and start working until lunch  in the mornings i'm most often checking  on emails and other correspondences  as well as just planning my day and the  rest of the week to make sure that i'm  on track to do what i set out to do  in the morning my brain is the most  fresh so after catching up on emails and  such  i kind of let it do what it needs to do  on this day i was researching a project  management tool to help me plan for  upcoming projects  and i also just decided to rearrange my  room i just wanted to do this that day  because i've been meaning to move this  organizer into the closet and felt like  it was a good time as i need to do so  and especially during quarantine because  your scenery doesn't change that often  i find that refreshing my space really  also refreshes my mind and soul  and now i'm just walking downstairs to  eat lunch  so at noon time i always eat lunch even  though technically i could eat lunch at  any time that i want  eating lunch at the same time every day  gives me some sort of structure and  routine to my days  i'm usually talking to scott during  lunch and just really appreciating the  food and unplugging from work during  this time  and after lunch i might clean a little  bit since we're all working from home  it's really hard to have that separation  between work and home  and so having these hours set where this  is work time and this is home time  has really helped me to maintain that  balance so then around one o'clock every  day  my afternoon work time commences usually  this means that i turn on my twitch  stream where i host co-working  co-studying co-coding streams it's been  really good to have this dream because  there's a lot of people in the same boat  who  join in on the stream they're all also  working from home and i feel like we've  all become kind of like  co-workers together we use the pomodoro  method to differentiate between work  time and social time  and we play kind of chill lo-fi hip-hop  music throughout  and so while i have the stream on i will  literally do work  in the afternoon i'm likely continuing  work that i started in the morning or  just starting something completely  different that's on my to-do list  usually my really time intensive work  happens in the afternoon so that might  be video editing or  coding but because the afternoon work  stretches so long i make sure to take  breaks in between  the pomodoro timer we use on the stream  certainly helps me to focus  but i also let my brain just kind of  turn off sometimes or peruse the  internet or learn something new  and that's why i wanted to thank the  sponsor of today's video brilliant  giving myself time and space to learn  new things throughout the day has really  helped me to avoid burnout  and stay inspired and creative brilliant  is a website that has a bunch of courses  in the sciences some of the courses dive  into really complex topics  and so it really helps me to really  think about new problems in new ways  they're all interactive and they break  down complex topics with great visuals  teaching you how to think and learn so  take a course on brilliant and start  your journey today  by going to brilliant.org slash hello  myuco and sign up for free and the first  200 people to go to that link will get  20  off the annual premium subscription  anyway  during the long stretch of the afternoon  where i'm working one of the things that  i do to kind of freshen things up is to  change location  on this day i had a meeting at the very  end of the day so  i went downstairs to just change my  environment  i made myself a very nice barley tea and  had a great meeting  [Music]  and then my work day concludes at around  5 30. so i hope you like this video  where i show you my work from home  routine in quarantine  make sure to hit that subscribe button  if you'd like to see more videos and  i'll see you next time  stay safe out there
 

